<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Sam Yang buys 12,500T of Chinese corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Sam Yang buys 12,500T of Chinese corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Sam Yang Co Ltd has bought 12,500 tonnes of Chinese corn at $144.30 a tonne C&amp;F, traders confirmed on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the corn was bought from Cargill through a private negotiation last Thursday.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for September 1-20 to the southwestern port of Mokpo.</p>
<p>Traders said South Korean buyers have bought 1.03 million tonnes of Chinese corn through private negotiations and tenders so far this year.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
